			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Route workspaces:getRecentlyOpened through WorkspacesRouter; consolidate remaining inline workspace dispatch\n\nAdd the `workspaces:getRecentlyOpened` route to WorkspacesRouter, delegating to the recently-developed `ReadRecentlyOpened` function for direct state access. This completes the recently-opened bookkeeping trio alongside add/remove/clear.\n\nReplace the remaining inline workspace match arms in DispatchMatch.rs (`getFolders`, `addFolder`, `removeFolder`, `getName`) with a single `command.starts_with(\"workspaces:\")` guard that delegates fully to `WorkspacesRouter::route()`. All four existing workspace lifecycle commands preserve their exact semantics — folder retrieval, folder addition/removal, and name resolution all pass through unchanged.\n\nPure structural consolidation with one new IPC command handler — no behavioural change to workspace lifecycle or recently-opened mutation semantics.",
			"SHA": "30b70a218595124841a0b795135555b201c5601d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T14:39:28Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1854,
				47
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Consolidate output, model, terminal, and extension host dispatch into routers; prune empty Dispatcher/ stubs\n\nContinue the modularization pattern established by SearchRouter, HistoryRouter, and ExtensionsRouter by extracting four additional dispatch domains from the inline match block in DispatchMatch.rs:\n\n- **OutputRouter** — routes all `output:*` commands (create, append, appendLine, clear, show, replace, dispose) into a dedicated module under Output/OutputRouter.rs.\n- **ModelRouter** — routes `model:*`, `textFile:*`, `text:*`, and `workspace:openTextDocument` commands into Model/ModelRouter.rs, preserving the Sky Tauri event relay for document open intent.\n- **TerminalRouter** — routes all `terminal:*` and `localPty:*` commands into Terminal/TerminalRouter.rs, carrying the full terminal lifecycle (localPty:createProcess, layout persistence, shell execution events, auto-reply rules) from the previously inline block.\n- **ExtensionHostRouter** — routes extension host lifecycle commands (starter, debug service, Cocoon message relay) into ExtensionHost/ExtensionHostRouter.rs.\n\n**WorkspacesRouter** is substantially expanded to include recently-opened bookkeeping (add/remove/clear), workspace identifier derivation (hash of first folder URI), workspace display name delegation, and dirty-workspace stubs — replacing the earlier thin wrapper that only handled folder retrieval and enter/create/delete.\n\n**Dispatcher/ module** is stripped: all 31 per-domain stub files deleted and the mod.rs reduced to a doc comment noting dispatch now lives inline in DispatchMatch.rs. The deleted stubs had been empty shells since the original Consolidation pass — their function-level handlers were already imported directly.\n\nDispatchMatch.rs imports are cleaned up: Model, Output, and TextFile function imports removed, replaced by the corresponding router path. The new dispatch arms use `command.starts_with(\"...\")` guards with `unwrap_or_else(|| Ok(Value::Null))` fallback, matching the convention established by SearchRouter and HistoryRouter.\n\nPure structural consolidation — no behavioural change to output channels, text model lifecycle, terminal PTY semantics, extension host debugging, or workspace folder/recently-opened handling.",
			"SHA": "1b4f8f6e8dcc4d3a4b57db2e804594b27c889359"
		},
